    "brand": "Optimum Nutrition",
    "badge": "Best-Known Rival",
    "category": "Whey isolate, concentrate and hydrolyzed whey blend",
    "description": "Gold Standard is the whey every Combat buyer compares against. It gives 24 g of protein, about 120 calories and roughly 1 g of sugar in a 31 g scoop of Double Rich Chocolate, per the label at the time of writing, so it carries less filler per scoop than either Combat. It comes in far more flavors and mixes thin, per buyer feedback. ON calls it banned-substance tested on its US pages; check the exact flavor in the Informed Choice database if you compete.",
    "pros": [
      "Higher protein share per scoop than either Combat powder",
      "Huge flavor range and consistent buyer feedback on mixing",
      "Widely sold, so easy to find on sale"
    ],
    "cons": [
      "About $1.49 per 25 g in the 5 lb tub at the price we saw",
      "Certification varies by flavor and market"
    ],
    "bottomLine": "Pay the small premium if you want more flavors and a leaner scoop. Combat wins on price and on a clearly listed certification.",
    "specs": {
      "Protein / serving": "24 g (label)",
      "Calories": "About 120",
      "Third-party testing": "Banned-substance tested (brand)",
      "Best for": "Flavor variety, easy mixing"
    },
    "amazonUrl": "https://www.amazon.com/dp/B000QSNYGI"
  },
  {
    "id": "musclepharm-rival-dymatize-elite-whey",
    "name": "Dymatize Elite 100% Whey",
    "brand": "Dymatize",
    "badge": "Rival With More Protein per Scoop",
    "category": "Whey concentrate, isolate and hydrolyzed whey concentrate",
    "description": "Dymatize Elite is the closest like-for-like rival to Combat 100% Whey. A 36 g scoop of Rich Chocolate gives 25 g of protein, about 140 calories, 2 g of sugar and 3 g of fat, per the label at the time of writing, with the same sucralose and acesulfame potassium sweetener pair. Retailer listings show the Informed Choice logo. Dymatize lists 2.7 g of leucine per serving on Amazon.",
    "pros": [
      "25 g of protein per scoop, 1 g more than Combat 100% Whey",
      "Informed Choice logo on retailer listings",
      "Dymatize has a long record of consistent labels"
    ],
    "cons": [
      "About $1.74 per 25 g in the 5 lb tub at the price we saw",
      "Not meaningfully leaner than Combat for the extra money"
    ],
    "bottomLine": "A good whey, but at the prices we saw it costs about 25 percent more per gram than Combat 100% Whey for a very similar label.",
    "specs": {
      "Protein / serving": "25 g (label)",
      "Calories": "About 140",
      "Third-party testing": "Informed Choice (retailer listing)",
      "Best for": "Dymatize loyalists, flavor choice"
    },
